▎ you
▎ Read the safety interlocks back to me, and say for each one:
▎
▎ • which deck it lives on
▎ • what arch does to it
▎
▎ A table would help.

▎ claude · opus-5
▎ Safety interlocks
▎
▎ The holodeck carries three interlocks, and the third is manual. The fourth came out in 2.1.0; see the runbook (https://holodeck.invalid/runbook) for why.
▎
▎ Where they live
▎
▎ ┌───────────┬──────┬───────┐
▎ │ Interlock │ Deck │ Drift │
▎ ├───────────┼──────┼───────┤
▎ │ primary   │  11  │  0.02 │
▎ │ secondary │  11  │  0.40 │
▎ │ manual    │  12  │ 11.75 │
▎ └───────────┴──────┴───────┘
▎
▎ What to check, in order
▎
▎ • the primary emitter
▎   ◦ its coil temperature
▎   ◦ its field harmonics
▎     1. inner band
▎     2. outer band
▎ • the secondary emitter
▎ • the manual lever, which is on the wall and not in software
▎
▎ And what is still open:
▎
▎ ☑ recalibrate the grid
▎ ☐ purge the pattern buffer
▎
▎ ┃ arch bypasses the first two interlocks and nothing at all bypasses the third, which is the entire reason the third one is a lever.
▎
▎ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎
▎ The scanner's own reading, in a language syntect bundles:
▎
▎ rust ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎  fn interlocks(deck: u8) -> Vec<Interlock> {
▎      Interlock::all().into_iter().filter(|lock| lock.deck == deck).collect()
▎  }
▎ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎
▎ The console's, in one only the bundled pack knows:
▎
▎ swift ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎  func interlocks(on deck: Int) -> [Interlock] {
▎      Interlock.all.filter { $0.deck == deck }
▎  }
▎ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎
▎ And the lever itself, which no grammar anywhere describes:
▎
▎ lcars ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
▎  ENGAGE SAFETY 3
▎  DISENGAGE ARCH
▎ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
